.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 4, 2026
.Dt MK.RESOLVED.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.resolved.mk
.Nd stops a build whose settings were changed too late
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Checks that
.Va TOOLCHAIN , ABI , TARGET , TARGET_ARCH , OPENMP
and
.Va SANITIZE
still have the value
.Xr mk.common.mk 5
resolved them with.
Those settings choose the compiler, the flags and the build directory when
.Xr mk.common.mk 5
is read, so a change after that has no effect.
Rather than let the build go on with the old value, it stops with an error such
as:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
TOOLCHAIN=gcc was set after mk.common.mk had already resolved
TOOLCHAIN=llvm -- a module makefile or a mk/pre*.mk hook changed it
too late to have any effect ...
.Ed
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
Each role file reads it after the
.Cm pre
hooks, so it sees a setting made by a module after an early
.Ql .include "mk.common.mk" ,
and one made by a hook file.
Setting the same value again is accepted.
.Pp
To change one of them, set it before the include of
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
on the command line, or in the environment.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.local.mk 5 ,
.Xr bmake-it 7
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
